Valid Scenarios
Select today's date from UI – e.g., 23-07-2025 → Should be accepted.
Select a date exactly 2 years ago from today – e.g., 23-07-2023 → Should be allowed.
Manually enter valid past date in range – e.g., 15-05-2024 → Should be accepted.
Clear date using Backspace/Delete and enter valid date – Should update correctly.
Paste a valid date (01-01-2024) → Should be accepted.
❌ Invalid Scenarios
Select any future date from UI (e.g., 01-08-2025) – Should be greyed out/unselectable.
Select a date older than 2 years (e.g., 22-07-2023) – Should be disabled in UI.
Manually enter date before allowed range (e.g., 01-01-2020) – Should show validation error.
Manually enter a future date (e.g., 25-12-2025) – Should be rejected.
Enter date in wrong format (e.g., 2025/07/01) – Should trigger format validation error.
Enter alphabetic characters (e.g., ab-cd-efgh) – Should be rejected or auto-cleared.
Enter partial date (e.g., 15-07) – Should not be accepted.
Enter non-existent date (e.g., 31-02-2024) – Should show date validity error.
Leave field blank and try to submit – Should show "required" error if mandatory.
Enter symbols/special characters (e.g., $$-##-!!!!) – Should be rejected.
